-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Phase 2 -- stats for the 467 Cataclysm set shells
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The set items downported by the Wraith run exist in item_template with the
-- right name, class/subclass, quality and slot, and ZERO of everything else --
-- no item level, no required level, no stats, no armour, no sockets, no
-- durability, no prices. This fills those in from the retail source.
--
-- SOURCE -- Cata 4.3.4 DBFilesClient/Item-sparse.db2 (WDB2, build 15595,
-- 54,086 rows x 133 fields), read through the wow-update-enUS-15211/15354/15595
-- StormLib patch chain, plus DBFilesClient/Item.db2 for class/subclass/slot.
-- Field layout verified against the live DB: item 51130 reads back ilvl 264,
-- req 80, quality 4, slot 3, set 898 -- all matching item_template exactly.
--
-- ARMOUR is not stored in Item-sparse; Cataclysm computes it from curves.
-- Reproduced here as
--     floor( ItemArmorQuality[ilvl][quality]
--          * ItemArmorTotal[ilvl][armour type]
--          * ArmorLocation[slot][armour type] )
-- and validated against stock ilvl-264 plate, which the curve reproduces to
-- within a point: 51130 -> 1981 vs 1980 stored, 51216 -> 2311 vs 2310. Tank
-- pieces carry extra armour in ArmorDamageModifier, which the client adds on
-- top -- that column is written through unchanged rather than folded in, which
-- is how stock rows store it (50968: 2642 base + 1176 bonus = 3818 shown).
--
-- WEAPON DAMAGE is likewise curve-derived in Cataclysm and is NOT written here.
-- Eight of these items are weapons: the two fist weapons of set 951 and the six
-- Dragon Soul legendary daggers (sets 1087-1089). They keep dmg_min1 / dmg_max1
-- = 0 rather than being given invented numbers.
--
-- FILE 04 COVERS THEM. The two fist weapons get their damage there, and the six
-- daggers -- which have no Item-sparse row at all in this build, so this file
-- skips them entirely -- are written in full from the Mists 5.4 world DB, the last
-- pre-squish source that still carries their true item levels and absolute stats.
-- Apply 04 after this file; without it those four sets ship with weapons that
-- swing for zero.
--
-- DURABILITY is in neither DB2. It is a fixed per-slot/armour-type constant that
-- did not change in Cataclysm, so the values come from the modal MaxDurability of
-- stock ilvl>=200 gear of the same (class, subclass, InventoryType).
--
-- MASTERY RATING (Item-sparse stat type 49) HAS NO 3.3.5 EQUIVALENT -- the
-- ITEM_MOD enum stops at 48 (ITEM_MOD_BLOCK_VALUE). 168 mastery stats across these
-- items are therefore DROPPED, not remapped: every affected item simply carries
-- one stat fewer. Substituting crit or haste for mastery would be a balance
-- decision, not a downport, so it is not made here. To change that, map 49 to
-- the desired ITEM_MOD in emit_phase2.py (DROPPED_STAT) and regenerate.
--
-- Deliberately does NOT write `itemset`: file 01 owns that column. Writing the
-- Cata value here would also set sets for the 10 deferred bonus groups, which
-- have no itemset_dbc row, and the loader would warn and force them back to 0.
--
-- The stat_type/stat_value pairs are written densely from slot 1. This fork
-- derives StatsCount at load time by counting non-zero stat_value entries
-- (ObjectMgr.cpp), so no count column needs maintaining.
--
-- FIELD VALIDATION -- several Cata columns have id spaces 3.3.5 does not have, and
-- ObjectMgr::LoadItemTemplates warns and zeroes them at load. They are corrected
-- here instead: ItemLimitCategory (3.3.5 tops out at 85 vs Cata 89-198),
-- RandomSuffix (ItemRandomSuffix.dbc holds 5-99 vs Cata 417-465),
-- RequiredReputationFaction (Faction.dbc ends at 1171 vs Cata 1172-1178),
-- socket colours (masked to META|RED|YELLOW|BLUE = 15; Cata sends 32), BagFamily
-- and TotemCategory/GemProperties. Material and Sheath come from our own client
-- Item.dbc, because that is what the server compares them against -- not from the
-- Cata source they were read from.
-- Corrections applied: RandomSuffix 16, sheath <- Item.dbc 2
--
-- Idempotent. Apply against acore_world; no worldserver restart is strictly
-- needed beyond the usual item_template reload.
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Items belonging to the 45 sets shipped in file 01 -- 242 items
-- -------------------------------------------------------------------------

